    "VISUAL_NAME": "Pie",
    "SCHEMA_NAME": "FAM_ASSET_VALUE_BY_CATEGORY",
    "SCHEMA_DESCR": "Management Dashboard tile VIS_005 — Asset Value by Category. FRS calls for a Doughnut-Chart of TOTAL_CAPITALIZED_COST grouped by CATEGORY_CODE, drilling to the Asset Register Report filtered by category. ASSUMPTIONS/GAPS (documented per non-interactive build instructions, no table/column invented): (1) Neither an Asset Category Master table nor a CATEGORY_CODE column on FAM_ASSET_REGISTER (deployed with only ASSET_CODE/ASSET_NAME/CAPITALIZATION_DATE) exists in this project, so there is NO deployed linkage from an asset to a category and TOTAL_CAPITALIZED_COST does not exist anywhere either — a true per-category asset-value breakdown cannot be computed. As the closest real, ungrounded-free data available, this chart plots COUNT(*) of currently-effective rows in FAM_DEP_RATE_CA_MASTER (the Companies Act depreciation rate master, keyed by CATEGORY_CODE) as a structural placeholder — it shows the category list is real but the measure is NOT an asset value; revisit once Asset Category Master + FAM_ASSET_REGISTER.CATEGORY_CODE + PURCHASE_COST/TOTAL_CAPITALIZED_COST are deployed, at which point this should become SUM(TOTAL_CAPITALIZED_COST) grouped by CATEGORY_CODE joined from the Asset Register. (2) Catalog visual type note: the runtime's 'DoughNut' catalog entry is a fixed 3-slot KPI achievement-ring layout (Total Value/Achievement Value 1-3), not an open-ended multi-category share-of-whole chart, so it cannot express an arbitrary-cardinality category breakdown; per the domain skill's own guidance ('share of whole -> Pie, or DoughNut for a KPI ring') this tile uses 'Pie' instead, the closest catalog visual that correctly renders a category-wise share-of-whole. (3) BRANCH_CODE/FINANCIAL_YEAR dashboard criteria are NOT applied here — FAM_DEP_RATE_CA_MASTER is a branch-agnostic rate master with no branch column and no transactional date; only a fixed EFFECTIVE_FROM_DATE <= CURRENT_DATE filter is applied to exclude not-yet-effective future rate records.",
